  "id": "classical-psychoanalysis",
  "term": "classical psychoanalysis",
  "definition": "Classical psychoanalysis is a form of psychological treatment that has traditionally aimed to bring unconscious conflicts into awareness mainly through spoken language, often described as the talking cure. In the source material, it is contrasted with newer psychoanalytic views that also stress bodily communication and pre-verbal interaction between patient and therapist.",
